-- title:
--   r-integrality of a quaternion with Hecke-integral finite idele
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_1,b_1$ and write $H=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ for the associated quaternion algebra, and $\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}=$ the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $R_1,O$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $H$ with $R_1$ an order in the sense of the project predicate `IsOrder`, i.e. $1\in R_1$, $R_1$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $H$, and it is finitely generated; assume $O\le R_1$. Let $r$ be a prime, $\ell$ a nonzero natural number, $s\in H^\times$, and $sf$ a unit of $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume first that for every height-one prime $u$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $r\notin u$, the component of $sf$ at $u$, obtained by applying the evaluation $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}\to H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_u$, equals $s\otimes 1$. Assume second that $h:=\delta(\ell)\cdot sf^{-1}$ lies in `primeHeckeSet` $O\,\ell$, where $\delta(\ell)$ is the diagonal idele attached to the unit $\ell$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ pushed into $H^\times$ and then into $(H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{Q}})^\times$ by $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$; that is, writing $\widehat{O}$ for the additive subgroup of $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes a$ with $z\in O$ and $a$ a finite adele integral at every place, one has $h\in\widehat{O}$, $\ell\cdot h^{-1}\in\widehat{O}$, $h^{-1}\notin\widehat{O}$ and $\ell^{-1}h\notin\widehat{O}$. The conclusion is that there exists $a\in\mathbb{N}$ with $r^a s\in R_1$.
--
--   This is the local–global integrality step in the quaternionic Hecke formalism: an element of $H^\times$ whose finite idele is integral for an order away from the prime $r$ is integral up to a power of $r$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd coset-graph and fake-elliptic-curve dictionary arguments, where Hecke correspondences at $\ell$ must be matched with global quaternions.
